 of safety.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 74%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $51.54 to $279 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Industrials peers: P/E 30.3 vs 23.3 and P/FCF 28.6 vs 22.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 34% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 3.5% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 3.6% (vs the 8% bar).","The 7 covering analysts target $138 on average, 79% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 7% falls short of the cost of capital of 9.5%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.51).","It runs a 14% gross margin and converts 5% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 2.86x.","ROE of 11% is amplified by 3.6x balance-sheet leverage (DuPont), so ROIC is the cleaner read on the business.","It spends 1.3% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 3.9x net debt to EBITDA ($156.1M of cash against $1.6B of debt), and interest cover is thin at 2.5x."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 29.3% over 3 years and 29.1% over 5 years, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 17%).","At current returns, reinvesting 84% of profits supports about 6.3% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 23.9% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.25 (orders outpacing sales), a backlog worth 78% of annual revenue and deferred revenue up 8%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.0x, 4.9% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 33, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.3%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Shareholder yield is a modest 0.5% (0.5% in buybacks).","The share count has grown 1.3% a year over five years, diluting existing holders."],"people":["With about 1,639 employees, each generates about $1.7M of revenue, 4.7x the Industrials median, and productivity has risen 22.5% a year.","That works out to $94K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.5M (2x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $23K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":48,"head":"Watch: LEAN BUY-rated, but the fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread) and it earns less than its cost of capital.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 43, gates 9/24)","Trades 40% below fair value of $129","Revenue grew 29.1%/yr over 5y","7 analysts' mean target $138 (+79%)"],"cons":["ROIC 7.5% vs WACC 9.5%","Net debt/EBITDA 3.9x","Interest coverage only 2.5x","Fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","P/E 30.3x vs sector 23.3x"],"flags":[],"need":["the fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)","it earns less than its cost of capital","too few checks pass (conviction 48)"],"buy_below":109.44,"vc":{"base":128.76,"base_src":"dcf","bear":51.54,"bull":278.67,"alt_median":19.42,"n_alt":1,"gap":5.6302,"dispersion":0.7379,"level":"LOW","why":["Monte Carlo spread is wide","models disagree (74% dispersion)","DCF is 563% above the other models' median ($19.42)","bull case is 5.4x the bear case"]},"med":{"pe":23.2692,"ev_ebitda":13.319,"pfcf":22.2778,"pb":3.0551,"roic":0.1001,"gross_margin":0.2851,"fcf_margin":0.068,"div_yield":0.0147}},"ticker":"ROAD","date":"2026-11-06"}